  "joint_derivation": "Per model, joints were derived from that model's own vertex clusters, not one fixed template: spine chain from Y-band centroids, Head from 85-100% Y centroid, Ear_L/Ear_R from top 90-100% X-split clusters around the head centre, Arm_L/R from 40-60% X extremes at chest height, Leg/Foot from bottom 0-15% X split with Z fixed to the bottom-band centre (so tail vertices do not pull a leg backward), Tail chain from the far-95% XZ direction in the 20-50% band (bayi/remaja back-right +X/-Z, dewasa mainly -Z) stepped outward with Y slightly down. Joint positions per model are in models[].joints, in glTF world coordinates (Y up, facing +Z).",
  "skinning": {
    "method": "Distance-based, weight = exp(-(distance/0.16)^2), top 4 joints per vertex, weights renormalized to sum 1.0. Inverse bind matrices are pure translations by -joint position, so bind pose leaves the mesh unchanged.",
    "attributes": "Mesh primitive JOINTS_0 (UNSIGNED_SHORT VEC4) and WEIGHTS_0 (FLOAT VEC4), Skin with 22 joints, skeleton = Root node, mesh node skin = 0, scene nodes = [mesh node, Root node].",
    "dominant_weight_share": "Vertices with a single joint weight >0.5: bayi 90.9%, remaja 85.2%, dewasa 79.8% (sigma 0.16)."
  },
