  "animation_priority": "sleep (isResting true) beats all, then idle_critical (hp < 30), idle_tired (hp 30-60), idle_fresh (hp > 60). tap_reaction and celebrate are one-shots over the active idle, then return to it.",
  "how_to_move_one_part_alone": {
    "principle": "Find the joint node by its exact name and rotate/scale only that node. Neighbouring parts will follow only through skin weights, they are not locked to the joint.",
    "three_js": "const ear = gltf.scene.getObjectByName('Ear_L'); ear.rotation.z += 0.35; // 20 deg, ear only. const tail = gltf.scene.getObjectByName('Tail_3'); tail.rotation.y += 0.35; // tail tip only. Do not rotate the mesh node itself if you want one part alone.",
    "unity": "var ear = model.transform.Find('Root/Hips/Spine/Chest/Neck/Head/Ear_L'); ear.localRotation *= Quaternion.Euler(0,0,20); var tail = model.transform.Find('Root/Hips/Tail_1/Tail_2/Tail_3'); tail.localRotation *= Quaternion.Euler(0,20,0);",
    "flutter_model_viewer": "model_viewer_plus selects whole clips, not single joints. For single-joint control use a Three.js/WebGL view, Unity, or Godot and address the joint by name as above.",
    "examples": {
      "rotate_only_Ear_L": "Ear_L rotation Z +20 deg",
      "rotate_only_Tail_3": "Tail_3 rotation Y +20 deg"
    }
  },
  "deformation_test": {
    "method": "Python linear-blend skinning on the actual JOINTS_0/WEIGHTS_0: rotate one joint 20 deg, compute per-vertex displacement, compare a region within 0.28 of Ear_L (ear) or 0.30 of Tail_3 (tail) against a torso region within 0.28-0.30 of Chest.",
    "results": {
      "momo_bayi.glb": {
        "ear_mean": 0.044587709954429545,
        "ear_n": 5144,
        "tail_mean": 0.024811703468210423,
        "tail_n": 3137,
        "torso_mean": 0.0,
        "torso_n": 1764
      },
      "momo_remaja.glb": {
        "ear_mean": 0.020564925220990696,
        "ear_n": 5531,
        "tail_mean": 0.01663667272264396,
        "tail_n": 6768,
        "torso_mean": 0.0,
        "torso_n": 7727
      },
      "momo_dewasa.glb": {
        "ear_mean": 0.020329456033562864,
        "ear_n": 3995,
        "tail_mean": 0.022244740400597866,
        "tail_n": 3213,
        "torso_mean": 0.0,
        "torso_n": 25120
      }
    },
    "interpretation": "Torso mean is 0.0 to 4 decimal places because torso-region vertices are not in the top-4 weights for Ear_L or Tail_3, so they do not move at all in those single-joint tests, while ear/tail regions move 0.017-0.045 units (mesh height about 1.9 units). Separation is therefore clean for these two tests, not just larger."
  },
  "honest_limits": [
    "Tail_1 (tail base) blends heavily with Hips/Spine: mean weight on its vertices is only 0.076-0.198, versus Tail_Tip 0.23-0.41 and Ear_L 0.25-0.58. Tail base motion is soft, tail tip motion is sharp. This is inherent to distance skinning on a fused mesh, not a separate tail mesh.",
    "Remaja Forearm_R covers only 2063 vertices in the top-4 set (versus 6244 bayi, 20633 dewasa), because its arm position sits close to Chest/Neck clusters. Its motion still works, but is more blended with Chest than the other arms.",
    "The mesh is still one fused primitive, so there is no separate eye, mouth, or ear mesh to blink or twitch independently of the head/ear joint. Eye blink and mouth shape still need a separate face mesh or morph targets, which this rig does not invent.",
    "Joint positions are estimates from vertex clusters, not artist-placed bones from the original Tripo rig. They are recorded per model above so they can be corrected in Blender if Hakim wants exact bone placement."
  ],
  "inputs": {
    "hp": "Number 0-100",
    "isResting": "Boolean",
    "stage": "Number 1 Bayi, 2 Remaja, 3 Dewasa",
    "tap": "Trigger tap_reaction",
    "mission_or_level": "Trigger celebrate"
  }
}